  "function_code": 85,
  "name": "Up/Down Counter",
  "description": "The up/down counter function code is a digital counter with separate inputs for incrementing and decrementing the counter. The count updates on a logic 0 to logic 1 (positive) transition on either input. External logic can be used to hold or reset the count. The counter can be set to an initial value upon start-up or following reset. This function has high and low alarm features. Each drives a separate output when the input exceeds the alarm value.",
  "description_lines": [
    "The up/down counter function code is a digital counter with",
    "separate inputs for incrementing and decrementing the",
    "counter. The count updates on a logic 0 to logic 1 (positive)",
    "transition on either input.",
    "External logic can be used to hold or reset the count. The",
    "counter can be set to an initial value upon start-up or follow-",
    "ing reset.",
    "This function has high and low alarm features. Each drives a",
    "separate output when the input exceeds the alarm value."
  ],
